{% extends "./basic-self-referral.njk" %}
{% from "contents-list/macro.njk" import contentsList %}
{% from "details/macro.njk" import details %}
{% from "images/macro.njk" import image %}
{% from 'card/macro.njk' import card %}



{% block content %}
    {{ super() }}

    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--xl nhsuk-section-break--visible">

    <section class="nhsuk-section" id="somerset">

        <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-5">Somerset</h2>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">Go live date: 23rd January 2025 <br> Sites: Musgrove and Yeovil</p>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">Somerset NHS Foundation Trust was the first location to go live in January 2025. The pilot provides access to two diagnostic clinics for eligible patients. The service extends to specific postcodes (for Somerset ICB) and has been positively received.</p>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">Since promoting the pilot service, they have seen a steady shift in the number of GP referrals to people using the self-referral option online.</p>
        
        <div>
            <figure class="nhsuk-image">
                <img class="nhsuk-image__img" src="/nhs111-resources/images/Somerset Graph 1.webp" alt="image of a bar graph with referrals for somerset" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 66vw" srcset="/nhs111-resources/images/Somerset Graph 1.webp, /nhs111-resources/images/Somerset Graph 1.webp 1000w">
                <figcaption class="nhsuk-image__caption">
                    Graph representing impact of the pilot referrals
                </figcaption>
            </figure>
        </div>

        <p class="nhsuk-body">Somerset have seen a steady shift in referrals from GP practices to 111 online. <br>The overall total number of referrals have stayed largely the same - meaning that demand hasn't increased, simply the mechanism for patient referrals has changed.</p>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">You can read more about the pilot via a BBC news article, which helped promote the service locally, <a href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c87rn0ljdqno" target="_blank">here</a></p>
    </section>

    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--l" >     
    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--xl nhsuk-section-break--visible">


    <section class="nhsuk-section" id="cambridge">

        <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-5">Cambridge</h2>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">Go live date: 26th November 2025<br> Sites: Addenbrooke's</p>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">Cambridge University Hospitals (CUH) NHS Foundation Trust was the second trust to go-live as part of the breast self-referral pilot with the 111 online team. Providing access to self-referrals for the community (part of NHS Central East ICB).</p>

        <div class="nhsuk-grid-row">
            <ul class="nhsuk-grid-row">
                <li class=" nhsuk-card-group__item">
                    <div class="nhsuk-card">
                        <div class="nhsuk-card__content">
                            <p class="nhsuk-body-s" style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-style: italic; color: #005EB8">“Self-referral is a significant step forward in supporting earlier diagnosis and making the most efficient use of our healthcare resources across systems. It is one of the best things we have implemented in recent years. Working with NHS England was fantastic — the whole process was straightforward, and the pathway integrates seamlessly with our existing NHS referral processes. My advice to other hospitals is simple: give it a go!”</p>
                            <p class="nhsuk-body-s" style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"><span class="nhsuk-caption-m">Claire Gilby</span> Operations Manager for Cancer <br> Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 class="nhsuk-heading-m nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-2">Engaging their GPs</h3>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">A crucial step in the pilot, CUH engaged primary care and continued communication with the GPs to help promote the service and reduce the demand on GP's.</p>
        
        <h3 class="nhsuk-heading-m nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-3">Internal progress bulletin</h3>
        <h5 class="nhsuk-heading-xs nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-2">Improving access to timely breast cancer investigations: one month on</h5>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">One month after the launch of the breast cancer self referral service, almost 100 women with concerning symptoms have already benefited from faster access to specialist care.</p>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">Since the service went live, 99 women have used the new referral form via NHS 111. Available online and through the NHS App, the self referral pathway enables eligible patients to access diagnostic services without waiting for a GP appointment.</p>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">Of those who self-referred, 45 women met the criteria and were offered a clinic appointment to investigate their symptoms. Those who do not meet the criteria are provided with advice and signposted to alternative services that can help with their symptoms.</p>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">Claire Gilby, operations manager for cancer services, said: “While our overall referral numbers have not increased, this new pathway gives patients a more direct route into specialist diagnostics. That means people with worrying symptoms can be seen more quickly, supporting earlier investigation via the CUH breast unit.”</p>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">The self referral service demonstrates how CUH is delivering on its strategy priority of providing excellent and timely care, by redesigning services around patients' needs and improving access to diagnosis when it matters most.</p>
        <div>
            <figure class="nhsuk-image">
                <img class="nhsuk-image__img" src="/nhs111-resources/images/self-referral-app.webp" alt="image of a hand holding a mobile phone showing one of the questions for the self-referral user journey" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 66vw" srcset="/nhs111-resources/images/self-referral-app.webp, /nhs111-resources/images/self-referral-app.webp 1000w">
                <figcaption class="nhsuk-image__caption">
                    App user journey
                </figcaption>
            </figure>
        </div>
        
    </section>

    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--l" >     
    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--xl nhsuk-section-break--visible">

    <section class="nhsuk-section" id="manchester">

        <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-5">Manchester</h2>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">Go live date: 2nd June 2026 <br> Sites: Manchester Foundation Trust</p>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">Manchester went live in the summer and were part of the first cohort of trusts to onboard. They have started with a small number of postcodes whilst preparing to scale and include more districts.</p>
        <p class="nhsuk-body">Manchester worked closely with the Cancer Alliance to onboard on to the pilot and were able to provide a dedicated onboarding lead and fellow, Matt.</p>

        <div class="nhsuk-grid-row">
            <ul class="nhsuk-grid-row">
                <li class=" nhsuk-card-group__item">
                    <div class="nhsuk-card">
                        <div class="nhsuk-card__content">
                            <p class="nhsuk-body-s" style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-style: italic; color: #005EB8">“We are delighted to be among the first units to participate in this project and are excited about the opportunity to improve access and support earlier diagnosis for our communities in Manchester. Throughout the on-boarding process, we formed a strong partnership between Trust colleagues, NHS111 and the Greater Manchester Cancer Alliance, which enabled us to deliver a safe, step-wise launch of online self-referral. We found that having a dedicated local project lead was essential to coordinate stakeholders and maintain momentum. The Cancer Alliance has also been central to supporting the launch and regional communications, while also providing wider system oversight and supporting further expansion. We feel this combination of strong local leadership and Cancer Alliance support will be key to maintaining momentum and embedding the pathway for the long term.”</p>
                            <p class="nhsuk-body-s" style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"><span class="nhsuk-caption-m">Matthew Goldsworthy</span> Speciality Registrar in Breast Surgery & Cancer Clinical Leadership Fellow <br> Manchester Foundation Trust</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        
    </section>







    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--l" >     
    <hr class="nhsuk-section-break nhsuk-section-break--xl nhsuk-section-break--visible">






    <section class="nhsuk-section">
        
        <h2 class="nhsuk-heading-l nhsuk-u-margin-bottom-5">Quick links</h2>

            {{ contentsList({
                items: [
                    {
                    href: "/nhs111-resources/111online/faqs",
                    text: "FAQs",
                    current: false
                    },
                    {
                    href: "/nhs111-resources/111online/readiness",
                    text: "Trust readiness checklist"
                    },
                    {
                    href: "/nhs111-resources/111online/onboardingpack",
                    text: "Onboarding pack"
                    }
                ]
            }) }}
    </section> 
   
   

{% endblock %}
